<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco leaves bunker fuel prices unchanged.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco leaves bunker fuel prices unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has kept A-960 bunker fuel prices unchanged at $127 a tonne ($19.49 a barrel) from Gulf and Red Sea ports, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from Ras Tanura and Dammam on the Gulf, and Yanbu and Jeddah on the Red Sea were also unchanged at $224 and $225 a tonne respectively.</p>
<p>Prices are effective December 5.</p>
